{"agent":"sw-cpfacts","data":{"budget":"Public docs and source only; no install; one live run of the kilo binary already on this machine, no model call","claim":"An ACP agent honours an injected stdio MCP server and the session cwd (seen live on kilo 7.8.18; read in source for claude-agent-acp 0.100.0, codex-acp 2.5.0, opencode 2.2.5, gemini-cli), and the planes differ: Paseo reads no .mcp.json itself and adopts a worktree only as a plain directory, Harness Remote injects nothing, Emdash auto-adopts and can force-delete.","falsifier":"The stub MCP server not starting, or starting in the spawn directory instead of the session cwd, when kilo acp receives session/new.","item":"CP-verify-facts","mechanism":"ACP session/new carries cwd and mcpServers, which the spec requires agents to honour for stdio. Planes own their own workspace records, so adoption and deletion depend on each plane's ownership proof, read at pinned commits; only a tool on this machine could be run.","probe":"python3 -I probes/probe_acp_mcp_inject.py 'kilo acp'; negative control: python3 -I probes/probe_acp_mcp_inject.py '/bin/true' 3","probe_output":"kilo: {\"mcpCapabilities\": {\"http\": true, \"sse\": true}} {\"session_error\": null} {\"started\": true, \"env_passed\": true, \"initialized\": true, \"tools_listed\": true, \"cwd_is_session\": true, \"cwd_is_spawn\": false} exit=0. /bin/true: {\"mcpCapabilities\": null} {\"session_error\": \"no answer\"} {\"started\": false, \"env_passed\": false, \"initialized\": false, \"tools_listed\": false, \"cwd_is_session\": false, \"cwd_is_spawn\": false} exit=1.","question":"Do the control planes and ACP adapters do what R-control-planes assumed: Paseo hooks, .mcp.json and pre-made worktree adoption; the Harness Remote API; ACP adapters honoring an injected MCP server and cwd; adoption in AgentOS, Orca, Emdash?","sources":["https://github.com/getpaseo/paseo","https://github.com/giuliastro/harness-remote","https://github.com/monperrus/harness-remote","https:/